<article class="env-lemma" id="03R6">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03R6">Lemma <span data-tag="03R6">59.61.5</span>.</a> Let $K$ be a field and let $K^{sep}$ be a separable algebraic closure. Then the set of isomorphism classes of central simple algebras of degree $d$ over $K$ is in bijection with the non-abelian cohomology $H^1(\text{Gal}(K^{sep}/K), \text{PGL}_ d(K^{sep}))$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Sketch of proof..</strong>
       The Skolem-Noether theorem (see Brauer Groups, Theorem <a href="/tag/074Q" data-tag="074Q">11.6.1</a>) implies that for any field $L$ the group $\text{Aut}_{L\text{-Algebras}}(\text{Mat}_ d(L))$ equals $\text{PGL}_ d(L)$. By Theorem <a href="/tag/03R2" data-tag="03R2">59.61.1</a>, we see that central simple algebras of degree $d$ correspond to forms of the $K$-algebra $\text{Mat}_ d(K)$. Combined we see that isomorphism classes of degree $d$ central simple algebras correspond to elements of $H^1(\text{Gal}(K^{sep}/K), \text{PGL}_ d(K^{sep}))$. For more details on twisting, see for example <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/SilvermanEllipticCurves">SilvermanEllipticCurves</a>]</span>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>